Native inference engine: vpipe
  https://github.com/tgo-app-dev/vpipe
  Base source: f34e2cc3a3adae759eea254419f436f5b7800057
  Copyright 2026 T-Go LLC. Apache-2.0.
  This product includes software developed at T-Go LLC.
  The release redistributes a modified engine built from this base and the
  patches in tools/engine-patches, with the CLI filename changed to h3-engine.
  Changes add fixed compute selection, VAE operation fusion and H256 W8A8
  decoder projections. Version 0.7.0 also includes the RoPE precision
  correction following upstream and Turbo BF16 premerge before W8G64 preparation,
  with mapped-tensor lifetime and double-application guards. Native SOL/Sage
  attention remains upstream work. Upstream ownership and notices are retained.
  See docs/releases/0.7.0.md for the code/idea contribution map and scoped evidence.
  The exact modified revision is pinned in src/h3_apple/data/engine.json.
  Full license: licenses/vpipe-APACHE-2.0.txt
  Required notice: licenses/vpipe-NOTICE.txt
  Dependency notices: licenses/vpipe-THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt
  The engine archive also carries these three files. FFmpeg is installed
  separately through conda-forge, not bundled into the h3-apple wheel or engine
  archive. Its Conda packages retain their FFmpeg and codec-library licenses
  and build provenance:
  https://github.com/conda-forge/ffmpeg-feedstock
  https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

H256 rotated INT8 linear algorithm reference: Comfy Kitchen
  https://github.com/Comfy-Org/comfy-kitchen
  comfy_kitchen/backends/cuda/ops/int8_linear.cu (Apache-2.0).
  The h3-apple implementation uses native Metal integer matrix operations.
  No CUDA binary is bundled; Comfy performance measurements are not claimed
  as h3-apple results. Apache-2.0 text is included in LICENSE.

